#. type: Content of: <chapter><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/installing.xml:14
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This chapter contains instructions to build and configure a graphical user "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <chapter><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/installing.xml:57
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For a long time the only graphical environment usable with GNU/Linux has "
"been the <emphasis>X Window System</emphasis>. It uses a client/server model"
" which allows writing applications completely independent of the graphical "
"hardware. This has the drawback that accessing modern hardware acceleration "
"is difficult, so another approach named <emphasis>Wayland</emphasis> is "
"developed.  It is a simpler replacement for X, easier to develop and "
"maintain, using the OpenGL framework. The main desktop environments GNOME "
"and KDE have been ported to it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <chapter><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/installing.xml:69
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This chapter provides the basic components of the X Window System and "
"Wayland. For X, the chosen implementation is Xorg, which is a modular "
"implementation and requires more than 100 packages to be installed.  The "
"distribution of Xorg is given a release number by the developers, in this "
"case Xorg-&xorg-version;. Individual packages are updated as needed without "
"changing this number."
msgstr ""
